</tabber>'''Rita Repulsa''' is a female humanoid sorceress who was once bent on intergalactic domination and served as one of the leaders of the [[:Category:Evil Space Aliens|Evil Space Aliens]] and later joins the [[:Category:United Alliance of Evil|United Alliance of Evil]]. She's later purified into the '''Mystic Mother''' while her evil essence returns in the form of '''Robo Rita''' after possessing [[Alpha 8]].

==History==
===Past===
===Return to Earth===
[[File:MM Rita Repulsa Happy Birthday Zack.png|left|thumb|220x220px|Rita searching her book for a monster.]]
Rita had been sealed in her dumpster for nearly 10,000 years before it found its way back to the Moon. Not long after, a pair of [[Astronauts|curious astronauts]] stumbled upon the strange container and broke the seal that kept Rita's evil at bay. Released from her prison, she destroyed the dumpster and quickly set her sights on [[Earth]]. Reoccupying her palace which had lay vacant for eons, Rita sent her chief warrior, [[Goldar]], to Earth to lay siege to the world. However, Rita was met by her opponent [[Zordon]], who had managed to reestablish contact with Earth and gather new warriors. Beginning her second invasion of the planet, Rita's monsters were constantly defeated by Zordon's [[:Category:Mighty Morphin Power Rangers|Power Rangers]], teenage humans who wielded the mighty [[Power Coins]]. {{Storylink|Day of the Dumpster}}
[[File:MM Rita Repulsa Switching Places.png|right|thumb|220x220px|Rita watching the Rangers battle her giant monster.]]
While Rita largely relied on monsters created by her loyal minion [[Finster]] or with the help of other mystic allies such as [[Madame Woe]] or [[Lokar]], her master stroke came in creating a sixth Ranger to combat Zordon's warriors. Rita secured a [[Powerdraining Candle|Green Candle]] from the [[Wizard of Deception]] to aid in her next scheme.

Having long ago come into the possession of a Power Coin, Rita selected one of the Rangers' own classmates, [[Tommy Oliver]], to become her [[Mighty Morphin Green Ranger|Green Ranger]]. While this proved effective for a time, Rita's plan was ultimately foiled when the Rangers broke her spell and brought Tommy back to the side of good. {{Storylink|Green With Evil}}

===Banished===
A year after being freed from her dumpster Rita was horrified when a storm of dark energy began to erupt throughout surrounding space. A storm, a manifestation of Lord Zedd's power, ends when the master of evil took up residence in the Palace's Chamber of Command. Disgusted with Rita's performance and her inability to conquer the Earth after several millennia, Zedd had returned to destroy Zordon once and for all. Sealing her away once more in a space dumpster, Rita is cast back out into the void only to swear revenge. {{Storylink|The Mutiny}}

Sometime later, her dumpster crashed into Angel Grove, where it was found by [[Farkas Bulkmeier|Bulk]] and [[Eugene Skullovitch|Skull]], who proceeded to try to open it with their tools, only to faint in shock at the sight of the shrunk Rita when they succed. However, her freedom is short-lived due to the Rangers' arriving to the scene, who soon reimprisoned her in the dumpster and sent her back into space. {{Storylink|White Light}}

===Marriage===
Sometime after the demise of the [[Photomare]] and the destruction of the [[Rock of Time]], Lord Zedd has to enter his bicentennial Sleep of Oblivion to recharge his powers. However, Rita’s dumpster nears the Moon and soon explosively makes landing on the surface but she is unfazed and manages to escape from it. Rita enters via her old balcony and starts calling out for her former minions for whatever reason but gets no response so heads to the workshop of her only remaining ally; Finster. Finster has spent the last several months of his time idling away in his workshop and bemoans his complete lack of relevance now that Zedd is around. He has gone from monster-maker extraordinaire to a dolting old man alone in his workshop but then Rita appears in his workshop. Initially, Finster just passes her off as him hearing voices in his head but soon realizes that he isn’t and uses a potion to return her to her proper size with his Spectron Reintergrator.

Rita declares her intention to reclaim her own power so Finster suggests a monster army as he has had nothing better to do but Rita refuses. She tells him to create a love potion as she plans to brainwash Zedd into marrying her to regain her former glory without anyone being able to sabotage her. Finster comes up with the idea to use Alpha to trap the Power Rangers as part of Rita’s plan to give them to Zedd as a wedding gift which Rita happily accepts. When he returns from Earth after using two Putties to help restrain Alpha, Rita embraces him as thanks. Later on, whilst the Power Rangers do some dramatic wandering through the [[Specter Theatre]] and the doors slam shut. Finster applies a facelift to Rita which regresses her by around 10,000 years to make her look more appealing for Zedd. Later, whilst Alpha makes Zordon look silly and Finster recreates her favorite monsters to attack the Power Rangers, Rita goes to administer the love potion and manages to successfully do so without being discovered. {{Storylink|The Wedding|The Wedding, Part I}}
[[File:MM Rita Repulsa The Wedding.png|left|thumb|220x220px|Rita seduces Lord Zedd.]]
Rita lingers around in Zedd’s rejuvenation chamber, proclaiming that she will make Zedd redundant when she becomes his queen and seal him away in a dumpster, like he did to her once she controls Earth. Eventually, she makes Zedd wake up using a feather and he immediately begins flirting with her and being overly goofy. Goldar appears after being summoned by Zedd and immediately orders the Putties to seize her, but Lord Zedd stops him, much to his shock. Much to Goldar’s abject horror, Zedd then announces his plans to marry Rita which Goldar is helpless to stop and is even ordered to plan said wedding much to Rita’s intense delight. Whilst the [[Robogoat]] and the [[Snizzard]] chase down the Power Rangers, Rita goes to Finster and demands more monsters for her wedding with the specification that they give her a lot of gifts. Shortly thereafter, Rita and Zedd hold a toast of dry ice to their wedding but the Power Rangers then escape the Specter Theatre so Zedd drops everything and enlarges the [[Peckster]] and the [[Rhinoblaster]] after Rita comes up with the idea. The enlarged monsters easily defeat the [[Thunder Megazord (Mighty Morphin)#Thunderzords|Thunderzords]] and Alpha sends them back to the Specter Theatre. With the Power Rangers recontained, Rita has Finster do her make-up as she powders her face and complains about marrying Zedd although she tells him to select two monsters and send some [[Putty Patrollers|Putties]] to guard the Power Rangers and stop another escape. With both the Peckster and the Rhinoblaster standing guard, Lord Zedd begins his wedding ceremony with his monsters as guests and witnesses. {{Storylink|The Wedding|The Wedding Part II}}

Inside Serpentera, Rita sits back on Lord Zedd’s command chair whilst Zedd pilots the Zord towards Earth. Shortly thereafter however, just as Rita and Zedd begin a game of “99 bottles of Slime on the Wall," Goldar discovers that the Power Rangers have outsmarted the immensely dense Peckster and the Rhinoblaster and have escaped. He reports this to his masters and Zedd orders him to send the entire monster army to Earth to cut them off. Goldar sends the entire monster army along with Putties to Earth but they end up slipping away and the Robogoat even ends up accidentally flailing when the [[Lizzinator]]. The two villains watch in glee as the Rangers flee to the Command Center while being pursued by the monsters but manage to make it to the building and makes the pursuit a dismal failure. As such, Lord Zedd throws his Growth Bombs to enlarge the monster army in order to force the Rangers into a Zord fight where the monster army can annihilate them. However, they are all soon wiped out and Rita and Zedd withdraw to the Moon Palace in disgrace. With the scheme a failure, Rita opts not to trap Zedd like she planned since she will need his help in the future. {{Storylink|The Wedding|The Wedding, Part III}}

===Married Life===
Sometime after Rita's marriage to Zedd, [[Scorpina]] becomes disillusioned with Rita and began to desire power so started to read her spell books. However, it was a trap (probably set to either test her loyalty or to find who had been breaking into her library) and she was banished to the [[Talos Dimension]]. {{ComicStorylink|Power Rangers: Soul of the Dragon}}

Sometime after her wedding, Rita gets the huff with Lord Zedd for unknown reasons but he wants her to consult the [[Ghost of Darkness]] to summon the [[Wizard of Deception]] and trap the Power Rangers in the past. After some presumed begging from Goldar, Rita consults the Ghost of Darkness and bemoans every time that they have banished the Power Rangers [[Island of Illusion|several]] [[Rangers Back in Time|times]] and they have always returned. The Ghost of Darkness states that Tommy’s leadership is the key to defeating the Power Rangers for good; kill him and the team falls apart. Knowing his keen nature however, he suggests creating a clone to kill him whilst the Wizard of Deception sends the other Rangers into the past. After he swiftly sends down the Wizard of Deception, Rita bows thanks the Ghost of Darkness before leaving and the being is never seen again. Later, after the Wizard of Deception brainwashes Bulk and Skull to get some hair from Tommy, Rita goes to Finster to gloat. She then reveals her goal; recreate the Green Ranger and destroy the Rangers for good (despite that not being her original goal). Meanwhile, despite Bulk and Skull failing, the Wizard of Deception and Zedd’s Putty Patrol put Tommy into a coma and create [[Tommy Oliver/Clone|Tom Oliver]]. Even with all of the cards seemingly in Rita and Zedd’s hand, the Wizard of Deception is eventually killed and this plan fails miserably. {{Storylink|Return of the Green Ranger}}

On the week of [[Angel Grove High School|Angel Grove High]]'s school president elections, Rita decides to take advantage of this for her own plans but Lord Zedd turned out to be sexist and claim her to be useless as a villain due to her gender. However, when he leaves to create his own scheme, Rita summons [[Squatt]] and [[Baboo]] as well as [[Goldar]] and reveals her plan to use an enchanted rope to turn them into intensely toxic rivals. After some poster sabotage between the two, Rita sends a letter to Tommy claiming that she has some information to bury [[Kimberly Ann Hart|Kimberly]] and sends down Goldar with the Putties who manage to capture [[Saba]]. Shortly thereafter, whilst the Power Rangers regroup at the Command Center, Rita goes to Earth with Squatt and Baboo and takes control of Saba by gagging him before having a dance for her presumed victory. Five of the Power Rangers confront Rita to get Saba back but she just mocks them before summoning the [[White Tigerzord]] to destroy the Power Rangers. Its superior strength gets the upper-hand against the [[Thunder Megazord (Mighty Morphin)|Thunder Megazord]] and nearly destroys it completely much to the villains' delight. However, Tommy uses an Electro Magnet to retrieve Saba so Rita withdraws herself and the minions to avoid being crushed under the Tigerzord's foot. {{Storylink|Best Man for the Job}}

Rita learns that Kimberly likes the [[Grumble the Magic Elf]] storybook and decides to banish her, Rocky and Tommy into it to leave the Power Rangers very weak and easy to destroy so uses her magic to do so. Rita also has an ally named [[Mondo the Magician]] within the book who she knows can destroy them for her so focuses her efforts on killing the Power Rangers still outside of the storybook. However, they later escape after the destruction of the [[Turkey Jerk]] by completing the story so brings Mondo out of the storybook but the Thunder Megazord reseals him and renders yet another plan a failure. {{Storylink|Storybook Rangers}}

===[[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers (Season 3)|Season 3]]===
Rita's brother [[Rito Revolto]] arrives at the Moon Palace to add his sword to their fight against the Rangers. He destroys the Thunderzords, but the [[Ninja Megazord]] easily beats him and the [[Vampirus]] which returns the war to a stalemate. {{Storylink|Ninja Quest}}
[[File:AR Rita Repulsa Hogday Afternoon.png|right|thumb|220x220px|Rita celebrates a brief victory.]]
Not long after Rito's arrival on the moon, Master Vile arrives to criticize his daughter's choice in men but his plan involving the [[Blue Globbor]] fails so he sticks around. {{Storylink|Master Vile and the Metallic Armor}}

Attempting to upstage Zedd in conquering the Earth, Vile uses the [[Orb of Doom]] to reverse time on the planet and turns the Power Rangers back into children but his plan is thwarted by the [[:Category:Aquitar Rangers|Aquitar Rangers]] and he leaves for the [[Gamma Vile]] in disgrace. {{Storylink|Alien Rangers of Aquitar}}

While they attempt to set things right, Rita and Zedd plot their boldest move yet: they will destroy the Command Center and steal the powerful [[Zeo Crystal]] for themselves. The plan is ultimately a failure; Goldar and Rito's implosion device does go off but the Rangers, Zordon and Alpha 5 escape to a fortified [[Power Chamber]] underneath the wreckage. The Zeo Crystal turns up in the rubble as Goldar and Rito lost it during their getaway. {{Storylink|Hogday Afternoon}}

===[[Power Rangers Zeo|Zeo]]===
Despite the setbacks, Rita and Zedd celebrate their most significant victory over Zordon's forces by throwing a massive party in the throne room. Their good feelings however do not last as the [[:Category:Machine Empire|Machine Empire]], longtime rivals of both Rita and Zedd, stage a coup and force Rita and Zedd to flee the moon in Serpentera. {{Storylink|A Zeo Beginning}}

Rita and Zedd eventually return and exact revenge after the Machine Empire becomes a laughing stock due to their multiple defeats by the [[:Category:Zeo Rangers|Zeo Rangers]]. {{Storylink|A Golden Homecoming}}

Rita and Zedd later have Finster build a missile to annihilate the Machine Empire after [[King Mondo]]'s defeat but it gains sentience as [[Louie Kaboom]] who breaks free of their control and assumes command himself. {{Storylink|Bomber in the Summer}}

With the help of a bomb disguised as a gift, the ruling family of the Machine Empire is temporarily destroyed and Rita and Zedd once again ruled the moon for themselves. Rather than immediately resuming attacks however, Rita and Zedd opt to go on holiday and return to take their revenge at a later date. {{Storylink|Good as Gold}}

===Turbo===
[[File:Rita Repulsa called Divatox Movie Pr Turbo.jpg|thumb|Rita Repulsa talking to Divatox by phone.]]
The couple opt not to resume their struggle with the Power Rangers and advise [[Divatox]] to do the same when Divatox calls Rita at night for advice on defeating the [[:Category:Turbo Rangers|Rangers]]. She advises Divatox to run and emphasizes this by telling her how annoying marriage is by having her listen to Zedd's snoring. {{MovieStorylink|Turbo: A Power Rangers Movie}}
[[File:Villains Hologram.jpg|left|thumb|Rita Repulsa as a hologram along with the other villains shown by the Blue Senturion.]]
When the [[Blue Senturion]] came to the present to deliver [[Millennium Message (transmission)|a message]] to [[Dimitria]], sparking interest in Divatox, she alters her voice to sound like Dimitria and asks the Blue Senturion to show her the message. The message revealed that by the year 2000, all the evil factions (Divatox, Rita and Lord Zedd, and the Machine Empire) would conquer Earth and equally divide its land.

Later, although the Blue Senturion manages to hold off the Rangers, they manage to hold him off long enough for [[Justin Stewart|Justin]] to turn him off. As Justin deactivates the detonator, he activates the message, sees the villains in the hologram (Divatox, Rita and Lord Zedd, and the Machine Empire), and the Rangers see the first part of it. Wanting to know more about the message, Justin reactivates the Blue Senturion, who has been reset back to knowing who is truly evil: Divatox. {{Storylink|The Millennium Message}}

===In Space===
====Dark Specter's conference====
[[File:Lord Zedd and Rita at Dark Specter's conference.png|left|thumb|Rita Repulsa and Lord Zedd at Dark Specter's conference.]]
Rita and Zedd join their comrades in the [[:Category:United Alliance of Evil|United Alliance of Evil]] under [[Dark Specter]] to mount a final assault on the forces of good throughout the galaxy. At a conference on the [[Cimmerian Planet]], Rita meets her old friend Divatox who is acting more arrogant than usual. Rita learns from Divatox that she has defeated the Turbo Rangers, the successors to the Rangers who have been giving Rita and Zedd trouble for years. Shocked, Rita turns to Zedd to confirm if this was true; to her horror, he explains that it is "kind of the talk of the universe now." {{Storylink|From Out of Nowhere}}
{{-}}

====United Alliance of Evil invasion====
Lord Zedd and Rita Repulsa initially argue with Astronema over her plan, but they agree to follow her orders when they learn that Dark Specter has put her in charge, Rita and Zedd attack a planet in the [[Vica Galaxy]] and capture [[Trey of Triforia]], the former Gold Zeo Ranger. Before victory can be achieved, Rita alongside Lord Zedd, sees that [[Ecliptor]] appears in the sky to announce that Dark Specter has been destroyed and that Astronema is now the Queen of Evil. {{Storylink|Countdown to Destruction|Countdown to Destruction, Part 1}}

====Zordon's sacrifice====
[[File:IS Rita Repulsa Countdown to Destruction.png|right|thumb|Rita after being purified.]]
The following day, after [[Andros]] the Red Space Ranger destroyed Zordon's energy tube, freeing a great golden wave of [[Z-Wave|good energy]] that goes through the universe, Rita screams for Zedd not to let it get her, but the wave finally washes over them. It destroys most of their army, but leaves her and Zedd alive as humans. Now purified, Rita expresses happiness that she and Zedd have been purified together and, at his request, engages in a dance whilst Trey looks on in confusion. {{Storylink|Countdown to Destruction|Countdown to Destruction, Part 2}}

===The Lost Episode===
Rita Repulsa was seen in archive footage, along with various Villains and Rangers, when [[Austin St. John]] and [[Walter Jones]] related about the Power Rangers' team from ''Mighty Morphin'' until the recently aired [[:Category:Galaxy Rangers|Lost Galaxy]]. {{Storylink|The Lost Episode}}

===Wild Force===
Four years after the fall of the United Alliance of Evil, [[Farkas Bulkmeier|Bulk]] and [[Eugene Skullovitch|Skull]] were playing [[:Category:Psycho Rangers|Psycho Ranger]] and [[:Category:Space Rangers|Space Ranger]] chess at [[Club Bulkmeier]]. Bulk mentions that he has known and met Lord Zedd and Rita Repulsa while having a conversation with Skull about the early days of Power Rangers. {{Storylink|Forever Red}}

===Dino Thunder===
Rita Repulsa is featured in a chronicle of Power Ranger history compiled by Tommy Oliver shortly after he forms the [[:Category:Dino Rangers|Dino Rangers]] which is found by the nascent Ranger team in the [[Dino Lab]]. Rita is mentioned as the inciting incident for Mighty Morphin Power Rangers as well as the one to make Tommy the Green Ranger. {{Storylink|Legacy of Power}}

===Mystic Force===
{{Quote|The Empress of all good magic, known as Rita in the dark days, she now uses her power to fight evil.|[[Udonna]] explaining to [[Clare]] who the Mystic Mother is.|Mystic Fate}}
[[File:Mystic mother.jpg|left|thumb|Rita Repulsa now becoming as the Mystic Mother, the Empress of Good Magic and leader of the Mystic Ones]]
Eight years after her purification, Rita is revealed to have regained her magical powers (assuming she lost them on her purification) and is using them for good. She became the Empress of Good Magic and leader of the Mystic Ones. As the Mystic Mother, she gives the [[:Category:Mystic Rangers|Mystic Force Rangers]] their link to the [[Morphin Grid]] and helps them in their quest to defeat evil mystic forces.

The [[Snow Prince]] arrives to warn her to flee but she refuses and attempts to fight off [[Octomus the Master|Octomus]] herself. However, Octomus proves to be too strong, and consumes her strongest spell, before attempting to kill her. She casts a spell on the Snow Prince to send him to inform the Rangers of what has happened and then is seemingly killed. [[Daggeron]] and [[Leanbow]] come to the Mystic Dimension to find her palace destroyed, the Mystic Mother missing and Octomus waiting for them. He defeats them both with no effort and then returns to Earth to destroy the Rangers. {{Storylink|Mystic Fate|Mystic Fate I}}{{Quote|The darkness is destroyed by light, and should it ever return, your magic must stop it.|Mystic Mother talk with the fourth wall|Mystic Force}}However, it is later revealed that the Mystic Mother has survived his attack by turning herself into energy before his spell struck her and then reforming herself. She later grants [[Clare]] the power of a true sorceress and encourages the Rangers immediately prior to their final battle with Octomus. Her last appearance is after Octomus' destruction, breaking the fourth wall. {{Storylink|Mystic Fate|Mystic Fate II}}

===Operation Overdrive===
Years later, [[Thrax]] mentions that he seeks to rebuild his parents' legacy, disgusted by the fact that they were "lost to goodness", when Thrax formed his Evil Alliance. Thrax introduces himself as the son of Rita and Lord Zedd and promises to be the demise of the [[:Category:Overdrive Rangers|Overdrive Rangers]].

Later, when the [[:Category:Retro Rangers|Retro Rangers]] defeated [[Flurious]] and his [[Chillers]], at the [[Hartford Mansion]], Adam is in the Control Center, trying to help Mr. Hartford with all the repairs. Mr. Hartford appreciates Adam's help. Adam tells him of his battles with Rita Repulsa and Lord Zedd. {{Storylink|Once A Ranger|Once A Ranger (1)}}

Thrax is determined to get the Sword Excelsior. He mentions that his parents Rita Repulsa and Lord Zedd were weak and succumbed to goodness but he will restore their legacy by destroying the [[Sentinel Knight]] with the powerful Sword Excelsior. Thrax approaches the warrior goddess and tries to take the sword but the goddess knocks him down. {{Storylink|Once A Ranger|Once A Ranger (2)}}

===Beast Morphers===
====Season 1====
[[Adam Daniels|Mayor Daniels]] expresses his dislike for the development of [[Morph X|Morph-X]] which he mentions Rita as an example along with [[Sledge (Dino Charge)|Sledge]] and [[Galvanax]] of super-villains wanting the Rangers' powers. {{Storylink|Beasts Unleashed}}

====Season 2====
[[File:Rita Repulsa in Scrozzle's database.jpg|thumb|Rita Repulsa in Scrozzle's database.]]
She was shown in archive footage along with the other villains in Scrozzle's database, when Evox's Army were looking for a past villain to revive with the [[Reanimizer]] and came across Lord Zedd.

When [[Scrozzle]] deems that Lord Zedd is the perfect candidate, [[Roxy/Cybervillain|Robo-Roxy]] is not sure. She recalls that Zedd could betray [[Venjix Virus|Evox]] in a heartbeat, showing how the former decimated the Machine Empire with a bomb present. That horrifies Scrozzle enough to change his mind, but when Sledge voices his agreement, [[Poisandra]] points out how Zedd was a better husband towards Rita than her own husband, leading to the couple arguing. {{Storylink|Making Bad}}

===Dino Fury===
[[File:Rita Repulsa legendary database.jpg|thumb|Rita Repulsa in the Legendary Ranger database.]]
[[Solon]] explains to [[Ollie Akana|Ollie]] that the Mighty Morphin Rangers never defeated Lord Zedd according to her. Ultimately, Rita Repulsa is briefly seen in a flashback via the [[Legendary Ranger Database]], during the time of Zordon's sacrifice sent the Z-Wave across the universe and purged the evil around it. That included Lord Zedd and Rita Repulsa being purified of their evil. {{Storylink|Unexpected Guest}}
{{-}}

===Once & Always===
[[File:Rita Returns In A Robot Body.png|thumb|Robo Rita]]
After Rita Repulsa was purified by the Z-Wave, her evil personality was exorcised from her body and converted into particles. During [[Billy Cranston]]'s attempts to resurrect Zordon, he accidentally awakened the evil Rita's particles and it landed onto [[Alpha 8]], creating '''Robo-Rita'''. Now in a new body, Robo-Rita began to threaten the Power Rangers once again after 30 years.

This form of Rita is deadlier and less comical. She is able to directly combat the Rangers, successfully kill [[Trini Kwan|Trini]], send Putty Patrollers around Earth to attack people and lure other Rangers outside of her adversaries, and capture them for a time machine she was creating to give knowledge to her younger self, so that she can kill the Rangers before Zordon could recruit them. However, the Rangers managed to finally kill this twisted essence of Rita, avenging Trini.

===Cosmic Fury===
An illusion of Rita was last shown with Lord Zedd after he "defeated" the Power Rangers, although it was only an illusional dream for the Emperor of Evil after he was banished to [[Nibyro]]. 

===[[Power Rangers: Soul of the Dragon]]===
Although only seen via flashback, depicting her kicking Scorpina into the Talos Dimension, Rita is mentioned prolifically throughout the book by both Tommy, [[Anara]], and the now purified Finster. She is the prime suspect for the recent outbreak of [[Power Coins#Power Crystals|Power Crystals]] that empower gangs but it is eventually revealed that Scorpina and her master Lokar are the real culprits.

==Personality==
<tabber>
Rita Repulsa=
During her days as an intergalactic evil witch, Rita Repulsa was a diabolical yet bad-tempered and unpleasant leader of her band of space aliens who speak in a screechy voice akin to storybook witches. Whenever her latest plan got foiled by the Rangers, she either cried out "I have a headache!" in dismay or was prone to take her frustration out on her underlings, or even both, even if they had absolutely nothing to do with what went wrong. Her most recurring victim of this abuse was Goldar which was evident in that he gladly switched sides with Lord Zedd out of his abuse and regretted the idea of brainwashing Kimberly to be an evil queen like her where she ended up behaved like Rita herself though the spell he used for latter deed technically only give her Rita's outfit and she successfully pretended to behave like real Rita.

Even in her youth, she set her own home ablaze just because she received a dragon instead of a planet like she wanted for her birthday, as stated by Rito. Rita genuinely loved her brother and father, Master Vile and sought to become an accomplished evil conqueror just like the latter. This motivated her in her fight against Zordon and, later, his Power Rangers, despite them foiling her plans time and time again. Not even being sealed into a dumpster twice, first by Zordon and then by her superior Lord Zedd, can extinguish her resolve. Although after her superior overthrow her and took over her band in the light of her recurring failures, Rita initially planned to overthrow Lord Zedd as she wanted payback towards him by using a love potion on him to make him fall in love and marry her. However, Rita changed her mind as Lord Zedd touched her heart and made her feelings towards him real. Their ability to feel love was arguably one of the reasons why she and Zedd ended up purified by Zordon's Energy Wave.

|-|
Mystic Mother=
After her purification, Rita became Mystic Mother, a kindly and wise practitioner of good magic. As the Empress of all Google magic, she is dedicated to protecting the magical realms and aiding the Mystic Force Rangers in their battle against evil.

Unlike her former self, the Mystic Mother demonstrates calmness, wisdom, and compassion. She possessed immense magical power and confidence in the strength of good magic, even confronting powerful forces like the [[Octomus the Master|Master]]. She beleived strong courage, emphasized that true strength comes from within.

She showed to be selfess and strategic thinking, transforming herself into energy to survive and later return to assist the rangers. She is bringing up, empowering others, such as [[Clare|Clare,]] and helping restore hope.

Despite her transformation, traces of her past remain, such as her occasional remark about getting headaches when things go wrong, serving as a reminder of her former self.
|-|
Robo Rita=
Robo Rita, an entity born from the surviving evil essence that was purged by the Z-Wave and assimilated Alpha 8 to form a body of her own, is bereft of her original self's personality quirks and redeeming qualities. As such, becomes more ruthless, having guts to face the Rangers herself and the capacity to kill.

Unlike the original Rita, Robo Rita shows patience and strategic foresight, dedicating significant time to planning her revenge against the Power Rangers. Her schemes are more deliberate, including attempting to manipulate time in order to eliminate the Rangers before they ever became Rangers.

By her calculated nature, Robo Rita is not without flaws. She can be petty and vengeful, reacting with excessive aggression when personally slighted, as in attempting to kill Billy in revenge for damaging her face. This lack of restraint highlights that, while more controlled than her past self, she is still driven by anger.
</tabber>

