==Behind the Scenes==
===Portrayal===
====Mighty Morphin Power Rangers====
*In the [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers (Season 1)|first season]] of ''[[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers]]'', the late Japanese actress [[Machiko Soga]] played the role of Rita via stock footage from the original Japanese show, ''[[Kyoryu Sentai Zyuranger|Zyuranger]]'', as well as specially filmed insert shots for the show. [[Carla Perez]] took over from [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers (Season 2)|Season 2]] through [[Power Rangers in Space|6]]. [[Julia Cortez]], an actress from Sydney, Australia, portrayed [[Rita Repulsa/1995 movie|Rita Repulsa]] in ''[[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie]]''.
**Carla Perez and Julia Cortez were cast at almost the same time, with one going on to portray the TV version and the latter, the movie version as they shot in Sydney, Australia.

====Voice====
*[[Barbara Goodson]] provided her voice in all of Rita's appearances through 1998, including both movies. When Barbara Goodson auditioned, she initially did a voice that imitated {{W|Billie Hayes}}' performance as Witchiepoo from {{W|H.R. Pufnstuf}}. But when told that she was not angry enough, she shouted at the directors, sounding exactly like what would later be Rita's voice, and got the part.
**Goodson was going to wear the costume when Rita returned in "The Wedding" and become her physical actress but the producers decided that she was too small to be Rita and cast Perez in the role as well.
*For the Japanese dub, Soga dubbed over her old ''Zyuranger'' performance.

====Mystic Force====
*In 2006, the character returned as the Mystic Mother for the end of ''Mystic Force'' and was played by Soga once more, and dubbed over in English by New Zealander [[Susan Brady]]. The footage was taken from ''[[Mahou Sentai Magiranger]]''. Neither character had any relation to each other besides the same actress originally. The writers decided to connect the two characters as a tribute to Soga, who passed away while ''Mystic Force'' was in production.

