Video Games=

===Mighty Morphin Power Rangers===
Goldar is a playable character in the [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers (Sega Genesis)|Sega Genesis]] and [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers (Game Gear)|Game Gear]] versions and is fought in the [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers (Game Boy)|Game Boy]] and [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers (Sega CD)|Sega CD]] versions.

===Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Fighting Edition===
Goldar is a playable character in ''[[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Fighting Edition]]''.

===Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie===
Goldar is a playable character in the [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie (Game Gear)|Game Gear]] version and is a boss in the [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie (Sega Genesis)|Sega Genesis]] and [[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: The Movie (Game Boy)|Game Boy]] versions.

===Power Rangers: Super Legends===
Goldar is the main villain in the Mighty Morphin' section of the ''[[Power Rangers: Super Legends]]''. He is first seen complaining about Rita making him do her dirty work once again. Suddenly, Lord Zedd appears in a time hole and tells him to contaminate Angel Grove's water supply, zombifying everyone there to form an army of Z-Putties. Goldar follows Zedd's demands, however the Power Rangers are hot on his tail. The "chase" ends at Angel Grove, where Goldar is ready to contaminate the water supply, however the Power Rangers stop him and he is forced to grow but he is defeated in the Megazord battle. In the game, he is voiced by prolific video game voice actor [[Nolan North]].

===Power Rangers Legends===
Goldar is an enemy in ''[[Power Rangers Legends]]''.

===Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: Mega Battle===
Goldar is the sixth boss in ''[[Mighty Morphin Power Rangers: Mega Battle]]''.

