===Power Rangers: Heroes of the Grid===
Goldar appears in the board game ''[[Power Rangers: Heroes of the Grid]]'' as an opponent in the Kickstarter Exclusive Deluxe Box expansion. He is classified as a Boss. Mega Goldar from the ''[[Power Rangers Legacy Wars]]'' video game and Goldar's Zord [[Cyclopsus]] (under the Cyclopsis spelling) are also in the board game sold separately as individual Deluxe Figure expansions and are classified as Giant Boss opponents.

===Power Rangers Deck-Building Game===
*Goldar appears as a playable character in the ''[[Power Rangers Deck-Building Game]]'' within the "Core Set" base game. A holofoil variant was given out as a free promo at Gen Con 2023.
*Various members that make up the United Alliance of Evil as a collective team (Rita Repulsa, Lord Zedd, Goldar, Finster, King Mondo and Divatox) appear together on a single playable "United Alliance of Evil" character card within the "Flying Higher" expansion. A holofoil variant can be found in the "Bonus Pack #3" promo card set.
*The United Alliance of Evil as a collective team (Rita Repulsa, Lord Zedd, Goldar, Finster, King Mondo and Divatox) can be found in the "Flying Higher" expansion as a Master card.
*Goldar can be found in the "Core Set" base game as a Master card.
*Goldar can be found in the "Flying Higher" expansion as a Villain card.
*Goldar's Zord Cyclopsus (under the Cyclopsis spelling) appears as a unique playable character in the "It's Morphin' Time" expansion. Unlike normal playable characters he does not have an empowered state. His giant sized card is instead only controlled by another playable villain character, but only if said character is both empowered and has in their possession the Pilot token. He can also receive damage in the form of damage tokens from the playable hero characters. If he receives too many damage tokens he'll be permanently destroyed for the remainder of the game.

===Power Rangers Roleplaying Game===
Goldar's Zord Cyclopsus appears in the ''[[Power Rangers Roleplaying Game]]'' as a Zord in the "Across the Stars" sourcebook.
